{
  "_comment": "🔣️ SSOT taxonomy vocabulary. Ticket 26/08/12/DISSOLVE-KERNELS-AND-MODULES-INTO-EVENT-SOURCED-ARTIFACTS: authored implementation lives at <semantic-collection>/<specific>/<file-kind-emoji>.<registered-extension>; reusable modules require two independent production semantic consumers at their lowest common owner.",
  "_semanticCollectionsComment": "🧩️ semanticCollections is the schema-first collection vocabulary. Every listed root uses semanticManifestFileKindId and semanticExtensionKey; semanticManifestFilenameOverrides may assign a direction-specific filename to one exact collection owner without ancestor fallback. Manifest members are in exact bijection with direct child directories. Collection roots are generated/mechanical assembly only.",
  "_standardsSubsetsComment": "Artifacts own standards only. Standards own subsets only. Subsets own schema, IO, and examples — never an engine: an artifact is data plus pure transforms, and behaviour belongs to the app that edits it (26/08/12/ENGINELESS-ARTIFACTS-AND-APP-STATE-MACHINES, #2553). Pure algorithms stay legal one level up, in a module's ⚙️engine — taxonomyLeafParentDirs keeps that word globally valid. Builder, analyzer, and composer remain types generated by derive_artifact_facets! / subset!, never filesystem facets. App examples under 🎛️apps stay app-owned.",
  "_subsetVocabularyComment": "🪆️ subsetDirPrefix/subsetSlugPattern/subsetAnyId/subsetAnyDirName define the default subset shape; subsetDirectoryOverrides gives one exact 🪆️subsets owner a complete logical-id to semantic-directory roster when siblings require distinct emojis; each standard owns its content vocabulary in the canonical subsetsManifestFileKindId leaf.",
  "_engineListComment": "Completeness/structural child dirs: artifacts declare standards; standards declare subsets; subsets declare schema+io+examples. Nested schema/io declared via schemaChildDirs, representationDirs, ioSemanticCollectionDirNames, ioDirectionDirs, ioDirectionChildDirs.",
  "_treePurityComment": "🌳️ Files use registered kind-only basenames; semantic concerns live in registered emoji-plus-slug directories. Package roots admit only exact contracts and recursively proven glue roles.",
  "_languageNeutralityComment": "🌐️ Language-neutral assets live at the owner root, never inside a package boundary; schema formats and package entries resolve through file-kind and exact-contract identifiers.",
  "_areaStateComment": "🗺️ Every declared and undeclared non-opaque area is clean-enforced. The actual compose and temp/compose prefixes are represented only by pathExclusions.",
  "_surfaceComment": "👁️✏️ Ticket 26/08/16/ARTIFACT-VIEWERS-AND-EDITORS-PER-SUBSET: a SURFACE is a subset-scoped UI binding with a role — 👁️viewer (read-only) or ✏️editor (mutating). Every OWNED subset carries both, beside 🧬️schema/🚪️io/📚️examples; a plugin may also mirror a FOREIGN subset's path to contribute a surface it does not own (contributedSubsetChildDirs), which requires a declared dependency on the owning plugin. Surfaces keep the mode/window shape 🎛️apps used, so modesDirName/windowsDirName/modeChildDirs/windowChildDirs are unchanged and now serve surfaces instead of apps. Sequencing (APA lesson 26/08/12): the surface* keys land FIRST and the app* keys are deleted only once the last 🎛️apps directory is gone — the Rust taxonomy assert! gate requires every listed facet dir on every plugin, so a flip in the other order panics all 33 plugins.",
  "_cleanMechanismComment": "🧹 Ticket 26/08/17/CLEAN-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-MECHANISM, wave W1 (allow-half only — W6 removes the old shapes). Target tree: artifact -> standard -> subset, each level ONE root 🦀️.rs that #[path]-mounts exactly its own child dirs and exports one declaration function (artifact()/standard()/subset()); a subset never `use`s a sibling subset or another standard. ⚠️ CORRECTED SHAPE (W1-E, forced by the W2-P pilot — supersedes the original import/export mirror this comment used to describe): `import`/`export` express DIRECTION, and direction exists ONLY for FOREIGN dialects, at 🚪️io/{📥️import/🧩️deserializers,📤️export/🧵️serializers}/🗿️artifacts/<kind>/🔖️<std>/✳️<sub>/ — because `ArtifactDsl` (parse+print) and `ArtifactPack` (decode+encode) are single, inherently bidirectional traits and Rust allows exactly one impl of a trait per type, so mirroring the SAME native codec under both import and export would force either duplicated codec logic (two sources of truth, the exact thing this ticket exists to remove) or one side being a hollow re-export. The NATIVE codec (text grammar + pack binary protocol) is therefore one bidirectional thing per facet and sits DIRECTLY under 🚪️io/<facet>/{📝️text,💾️binary}, unsplit, for all four schemaChildDirs members (📸️snapshot,🔺️diff,🧬️mutations,💡️inferences) — reusing schemaChildDirs x representationDirs rather than a new key, and reusing the existing ioSemanticCollectionDirNames + semanticCollections[\"🚪️io/<facet>\"] mechanism 🧬️mutations/💡️inferences already used pre-correction (now joined by 📸️snapshot/🔺️diff, all four direction:\"transport\" except 💡️inferences which stays \"export\"-only since inferences are derived, never imported), carrying the SAME spec filenames 🧬️schema/* carries today (📖️.grammar.semio / 📡️.protocol.semio / 🔣️.json). Anyone extending this vocabulary MUST NOT re-derive the rejected import/export mirror for the native codec — see the ⚠️ CORRECTION block in the ticket's 📓️design.md §1 and 📓️w1-e-report.md for the full reasoning. Shared code lives in 🔨️modules at the lowest common owner (standard -> artifact -> plugin -> ✏️s/🔨️modules -> framework), never at subset level. This wave adds 🔨️modules as an OPTIONAL (not required) child of plugin/artifact/standard roots — pluginChildDirs/artifactChildDirs/standardChildDirs grew the entry but pluginRequiredChildDirs/(no artifact- or standard-level required list exists) did NOT, so no completeness gate can fire on a still-missing 🔨️modules dir. The old 🧬️schema/*/{📝️text,💾️binary} entries stay valid meanwhile (both shapes legal during migration; W6 deletes the old one). Module-path slugs (policy policyOwnerMountsChildrenBreaches, script.ts policyModulePathSlug/policyStandardModulePathSlug): strip the emoji prefix, kebab->snake, a leading digit gets an underscore prefix (📄️txt->txt, ◻️2d->_2d, 🧊️3d->_3d, 🖐️5d->_5d, ✳️i-json->i_json); a standard slug (standardDirPrefix) additionally gets prefixed 'v' when it starts with a digit or 'v_' when it starts with a letter, with '.'/'-' folded to '_' first (🔖️1->v1, 🔖️1.4->v1_4, 🔖️89a->v89a, 🔖️ap214->v_ap214, 🔖️ecma-376->v_ecma_376, 🔖️riff-pcm->v_riff_pcm) — this is a pure algorithm parameterized by the pre-existing standardDirPrefix/subsetDirPrefix keys, so no new taxonomy data key was needed for it.",
